\par
The licence above covers MacroDeck's own code, which is the only thing this package installs \endash  a single file, MacroDeck.dll. MacroDeck uses the SOLIDWORKS API assemblies belonging to Dassault Systemes SolidWorks Corporation, but does not contain or include them: they are loaded when MacroDeck runs, from your own SOLIDWORKS installation. MacroDeck claims no rights over them.\par
\par
\b Worth knowing before you install\b0\par
\par
1. \b Pre-release.\b0  Version numbers below 1.0.0 are still under active development. Behaviour may change between versions.\par
\par
2. \b Back up your work.\b0  Save before running macros. As stated above, the software comes with no warranty of any kind.\par
\par
3. \b Macros are your own responsibility.\b0  MacroDeck only launches the macros in your library folder. What those macros do \endash  and their effects on your documents \endash  is down to whoever maintains that library.\par
\par
4. \b Reporting problems.\b0  Include the log file at %AppData%\\MacroDeck\\macrodeck.log if it exists.\par
\par
5. \b Unsigned installer.\b0  This package is not code-signed, so Windows SmartScreen will warn about an unknown publisher.\par
